WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.167
-Welcome back, everybody!

00:00:02.167 --> 00:00:04.934
We're talking with
the one the only Will Ferrell,

00:00:04.934 --> 00:00:09.467
who stars along Ryan Reynolds
in the new movie, "Spirited."

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:10.567
Will, welcome back.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.133
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:14.367
-I love your beard, by the way.
-You do?

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:16.400
-How great does his beard look?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.300
It's very flattering.
-I appreciate it.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.901
It's been coming in.
-Yeah.

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:21.801
-I went through puberty
last month.

00:00:21.801 --> 00:00:23.501
[ Laughter ]
-It's real, right?

00:00:23.501 --> 00:00:25.334
-[ Laughs ]
It is real.

00:00:25.334 --> 00:00:26.400
It was interesting.
We had --

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.234
Ryan Reynolds
was on Monday night,

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:30.000
and I said to him, I said,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.334
"I look like --
this is like a Spirit

00:00:31.334 --> 00:00:33.267
Halloween costume version
of Ryan Reynolds."

00:00:33.267 --> 00:00:35.200
Yeah, yeah.
He's such a good-looking man.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.567
But thank you.
-Yeah, he's gorgeous.

00:00:36.567 --> 00:00:37.868
-I appreciate this.

00:00:37.868 --> 00:00:39.100
I don't know
if I'm gonna keep it.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.734
You think I should keep it?
-I think so, yeah.

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:42.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
I think so, yeah.

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:44.067
-Saying keep it.
-It frames your face.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:45.601
I've seen your --
I've seen you with a beard.

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:46.934
-I've had a beard
every now and then.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.000
-Your dad had a beard.
-Yeah, my dad has a beard.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.400
-Yeah, he does.
He still -- He always did.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.067
-Currently has a beard.
-Yes.

00:00:52.067 --> 00:00:54.934
-That's his trademark look.
-Yeah. Beard.

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.200
-Yeah.
-Yeah, but you wouldn't --

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:57.534
would you --

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:59.100
You've had 'staches before.

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.901
-I've had 'stache--
I've had, like,

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:02.901
a thick mountain-man beard.
-Yeah.

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:04.634
Were you here -- Do you remember
when Forte grew --

00:01:04.634 --> 00:01:06.834
-A lot of bugs -- collected
a lot of bugs in there.

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:09.367
-Do you remember when Forte
had a neck beard?

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:11.901
-Did he just -- He shaved
everything but kept this?

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:14.033
No, I don't remember that.
-It was great.

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:16.601
He tried to make it a thing.
He shaved --

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:18.400
-Did it catch on?
-No, no, no.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:19.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:22.300
Bud, you had a big weekend.
Over the weekend.

00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:24.701
You have a soccer team,
first of all, with the LAFC.

00:01:24.701 --> 00:01:27.033
-LAFC --
Los Angeles Football Club.

00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:28.801
-Yeah, and -- and --
-And, yeah.

00:01:28.801 --> 00:01:31.167
-You won the first
Major League Soccer Cup.

00:01:31.167 --> 00:01:33.467
-Our first MLS Cup.
-You won!

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:34.901
-We won.
-You won!

00:01:34.901 --> 00:01:36.334
-Yes.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.334 --> 00:01:39.767
-This is a lot to celebrate.
-Yeah.

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.434
-But this is --
It was very exciting.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:42.701
It was down to a penalty, right?

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:47.167
-Went to overtime,
and we tied it up in the --

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:49.133
I don't know --
last minute of the overtime.

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:50.701
Then it went
to the penalty kicks.

00:01:50.701 --> 00:01:53.701
-How fun is this?
-And it was just crazy.

00:01:53.701 --> 00:01:55.767
-We have a clip of you
celebrating with the trophy.

00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:57.100
Take a look at this thing here.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:59.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:01.534
-Drinking from a cup.
-I mean, come on.

00:02:01.534 --> 00:02:02.834
What --
-Yeah.

00:02:02.834 --> 00:02:05.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.701
-That's a big deal
-And we had so many --

00:02:06.701 --> 00:02:09.501
We had Magic Johnson was there,
Sia was there.

00:02:09.501 --> 00:02:11.567
We have all this
wonderful family.

00:02:11.567 --> 00:02:14.067
Justin Bieber was there.
-No way.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.968
Yeah.
-Wait. What?

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.801
-Slay? Slay?
-Slay?

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.501
-What'd you say?
-Slay.

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:22.267
-Slay?
-Oh, it sounded like, "Baah!"

00:02:22.267 --> 00:02:23.334
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:25.033
Well --
-Like, is that a thing?

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:26.934
When you say Justin Bieber,
people go, "Baah!"

00:02:26.934 --> 00:02:28.167
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:30.601
-He has a lot of, yeah, fans.
-A ghost sheep.

00:02:30.601 --> 00:02:33.534
-Yeah, a ghost -- yeah.
Well, we invite every --

00:02:33.534 --> 00:02:35.734
We are allowed to invite
livestock to the show now.

00:02:35.734 --> 00:02:37.901
-Oh, that's great.
-It's a new thing we're doing.

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:40.334
2022 we started this thing.
-I love it.

00:02:40.334 --> 00:02:41.734
-And, yeah,
so animals love the show.

00:02:41.734 --> 00:02:43.133
-This show's so innovative.
-Yeah.

00:02:43.133 --> 00:02:45.133
I mean, we're just --
not just for humans, you know?

00:02:45.133 --> 00:02:46.467
-Yeah.
-We're for everybody,

00:02:46.467 --> 00:02:47.901
so shout-out
to all the sheep out there.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:50.434
-Yep.
[ Cheering ]

00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:54.033
-I noticed there's a very rare
California condor

00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:55.934
in the back row.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:58.567
There's only, like,
seven alive in the world.

00:02:58.567 --> 00:03:02.133
Yeah.
-There any cows out there?

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:04.067
[ Scattered mooing ]
-Couple over there.

00:03:04.067 --> 00:03:05.234
Couple over there.

00:03:05.234 --> 00:03:07.334
-Do we have any Bengal tigers?

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:09.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:12.200
-Oh, my --
-No Be-- No Bengal tigers.

00:03:12.200 --> 00:03:15.901
-No, no, I heard a baby --
-I heard a baby Bengal tiger.

00:03:15.901 --> 00:03:17.467
[ Imitating weak growl ]

00:03:17.467 --> 00:03:19.434
-Waking up.
Yeah, just taking a nap.

00:03:19.434 --> 00:03:21.434
They're waking up.
[ Both growling weakly ]

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:25.534
They're taking a nap.
-So cute, little baby Bengal.

00:03:25.534 --> 00:03:28.334
-Love a baby Bengal, man.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:29.934
-God, I wish we could
hold that baby Bengal.

00:03:29.934 --> 00:03:31.567
-No.
-No, okay.

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:35.100
Never mind.
-Where's the baby Bengal tiger?

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:36.868
I'll go find it.
I'll go find --

00:03:36.868 --> 00:03:38.400
[ Scattered cheers ]

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.267
Where is that baby Bengal tiger?

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:42.801
Come here, I hear you.
I found it.

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:44.567
Hey, how you doing?
Come here.

00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:46.067
How you doing?
Come on over.

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:48.334
Be careful.
Hey, be careful.

00:03:48.334 --> 00:03:49.968
-Oh.
-This is, uh...

00:03:49.968 --> 00:03:52.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Want to sit on his lap?

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:54.601
-Nice to meet you.
-Sit on his lap, I guess.

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:57.868
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:03:57.868 --> 00:04:01.267
-Oh, all right.

00:04:01.267 --> 00:04:03.601
Slippery.
Rawr!

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:04.834
-Rawr.
-How --

00:04:04.834 --> 00:04:07.534
-[ Hissing ]
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.534 --> 00:04:10.067
[ Growls ]
-Ooh!

00:04:10.067 --> 00:04:13.701
-How old is this, tiger, Will?
-Uh...

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:16.000
3 months old.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:17.133
-Can I borrow one of your pens?

00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:19.567
They love objects like this.
They --

00:04:19.567 --> 00:04:22.501
-Mreow! Mrow!
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.501 --> 00:04:24.567
-Okay. All right.
-This is how they learn to hunt.

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:26.334
-Be careful.
-This is how they learn to hunt.

00:04:26.334 --> 00:04:28.334
-[ Hissing ]
-Oh, be careful, be careful!

00:04:28.334 --> 00:04:29.767
Be careful, be careful,
be careful.

00:04:29.767 --> 00:04:31.100
All right.
-Oh! Whoa.

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:32.968
-Be careful.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.968 --> 00:04:34.434
-He --
-Be good.

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:37.033
-He's gonna -- He's gonna
get to be much bigger.

00:04:37.033 --> 00:04:38.801
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:38.801 --> 00:04:40.601
Now, did you have him on set?

00:04:40.601 --> 00:04:42.033
Well, I guess
he's only 3 months, so I mean...

00:04:42.033 --> 00:04:43.767
-He travels with me.
-He does travel with --

00:04:43.767 --> 00:04:44.901
-Yeah.
-And how long have you --

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:47.200
And he travels
to every premiere?

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.434
-Every movie premiere.
Uh, every family holiday.

00:04:50.434 --> 00:04:51.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:53.133
-Oh, my goodness.
-But he loves talk shows.

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:54.501
-You do?
-I do, I do.

00:04:54.501 --> 00:04:55.801
-You love coming to New York?
Oh, and you --

00:04:55.801 --> 00:04:57.601
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-You speak English?

00:04:57.601 --> 00:05:00.133
-He does.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:02.133
-Oh, my --
Oh, my God.

00:05:02.133 --> 00:05:03.701
-Yeah.
-Wow, that's amazing.

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.801
You taught him that.
That's amazing.

00:05:05.801 --> 00:05:08.667
-The scientific community
is going crazy over this guy.

00:05:08.667 --> 00:05:09.901
-They're going --
-They're going nuts.

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:11.667
-This is --
-He's, like, one of a kind.

00:05:11.667 --> 00:05:13.701
-This is absolutely something
I've never seen before.

00:05:13.701 --> 00:05:15.400
-Because I've had so many
Bengal tigers,

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:17.033
and none of them
could speak English.

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:18.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.434
And this is the first one.

00:05:19.434 --> 00:05:21.100
-Is the better for you
'cause you get to communicate

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:23.033
with other humans?
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:05:23.033 --> 00:05:26.133
I mean, they like it when I do
the -- [ hisses ] -- thing.

00:05:26.133 --> 00:05:27.234
-Yeah.
-But, usually, I mean,

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:28.868
they don't get what I mean.
-Yeah.

00:05:28.868 --> 00:05:30.901
-Yeah, I do the -- [ hisses ] --
and they're just like,

00:05:30.901 --> 00:05:32.734
"That's so cute," but...
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:32.734 --> 00:05:35.367
It means -- But it means,
"I want to rip your face off."

00:05:35.367 --> 00:05:36.534
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.534 --> 00:05:38.601
-Sometimes.
-So you speak English,

00:05:38.601 --> 00:05:40.968
but it also, you have
kind of an accent, as well.

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:43.300
-I do. I do.
Yeah, it's a German accent.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.033
-German, yeah.
-So it's a German --

00:05:45.033 --> 00:05:47.534
-I spoke -- I taught him English
in a German accent.

00:05:47.534 --> 00:05:53.334
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:53.334 --> 00:05:56.367
-You think -- You think teaching
in English would be enough.

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:59.067
-You would think,
but I wanted it to be distinct.

00:05:59.067 --> 00:06:00.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:04.767
-Yeah, but just speaking English
would make him rare enough.

00:06:04.767 --> 00:06:07.634
-Yeah, I just -- you know,
I just didn't know

00:06:07.634 --> 00:06:10.667
how many other baby
Bengal tigers knew English.

00:06:10.667 --> 00:06:13.467
And I thought, "Well,
if this becomes a thing,

00:06:13.467 --> 00:06:15.901
at least my guy speaks
with a German accent."

00:06:15.901 --> 00:06:19.334
-Yeah. Does your tiger
also speak German?

00:06:19.334 --> 00:06:23.601
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:23.601 --> 00:06:26.067
-Yes, the tiger speaks German.

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:27.868
[ Laughter ]
-Honestly, this is --

00:06:27.868 --> 00:06:30.200
-And he does, too.
-I do, too, yeah.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.033
-Oh, you do?
Could you say something?

00:06:32.033 --> 00:06:34.400
-Yeah, um...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.400 --> 00:06:35.434
Uh...

00:06:35.434 --> 00:06:37.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.234 --> 00:06:39.667
-You get embarrassed?
You get embarrassed?

00:06:39.667 --> 00:06:41.467
-Uh...
-Very quiet.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:43.567
-Der Spiegel.
-Der Spiegel, yeah.

00:06:43.567 --> 00:06:44.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.901 --> 00:06:46.267
-Beautifully said.
Beautifully said.

00:06:46.267 --> 00:06:48.701
-Yeah. Well, you want
to let him go back --

00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:50.100
-Should we release you?

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:52.334
Okay. Run, run, run!

00:06:52.334 --> 00:06:55.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:55.501 --> 00:06:56.868
-He made it.

00:06:56.868 --> 00:07:01.033
♪♪

00:07:01.033 --> 00:07:02.801
-That's amazing.
-Yeah.

00:07:02.801 --> 00:07:04.901
-Thank you for bring--

00:07:04.901 --> 00:07:08.100
Thank you for bringing him.
-I mean...

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:12.834
To -- To see them in the wild
is one thing,

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:15.367
but to really hold them
up close...

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:16.901
-That's something
I'll never forget.

00:07:16.901 --> 00:07:20.033
I've never been that close
to a Bengal tiger.

00:07:20.033 --> 00:07:21.667
Can we talk about "Spirited"?

00:07:21.667 --> 00:07:22.901
-Uh...
-Your movie?

00:07:22.901 --> 00:07:26.167
[ Laughter ]

00:07:26.167 --> 00:07:27.667
Let's talk about your film.

00:07:27.667 --> 00:07:28.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.801 --> 00:07:31.033
That's just amazing.
That was fantastic.

00:07:31.033 --> 00:07:33.000
But "Spirited" is --

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.234
I love this movie.
I love it.

00:07:34.234 --> 00:07:36.567
Ryan Reynolds.
-It's a musical.

00:07:36.567 --> 00:07:37.667
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:07:37.667 --> 00:07:38.801
-Singing and dancing in this.

00:07:38.801 --> 00:07:40.701
-A reimagining of
"A Christmas Carol."

00:07:40.701 --> 00:07:42.167
-I like the plot, by the way.
I love it.

00:07:42.167 --> 00:07:44.901
It's like the idea of
the Ghost of Christmas Present,

00:07:44.901 --> 00:07:48.033
but his -- his life.
-Right.

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:51.000
The viewpoint of the ghost world
and how, every year,

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.801
they pick a Scrooge to haunt,
but my character,

00:07:53.801 --> 00:07:56.634
Christmas Present, is having
kind of a crisis of faith

00:07:56.634 --> 00:07:59.667
and wondering,
"God, we pick, you know,

00:07:59.667 --> 00:08:01.667
a turd out every year
and try to convert them."

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:02.701
-Yeah.

00:08:02.701 --> 00:08:04.767
-"But is it really
doing any good?

00:08:04.767 --> 00:08:06.968
And why are we even
doing this anymore?"

00:08:06.968 --> 00:08:08.467
-"What is the point
of what we're doing?"

00:08:08.467 --> 00:08:09.834
-That's kind of
the thrust of the movie.

00:08:09.834 --> 00:08:13.467
-It's so funny. And by the way,
who did the music?

00:08:13.467 --> 00:08:16.634
-Pasek and Paul who --
-"La La Land."

00:08:16.634 --> 00:08:18.234
-"The Greatest Showman."
-"Greatest Showman."

00:08:18.234 --> 00:08:19.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:19.267 --> 00:08:21.167
-They are brilliant.
Every song is...

00:08:21.167 --> 00:08:23.334
-Yeah.
-...so catchy, so funny.

00:08:23.334 --> 00:08:25.467
-But we really had to sing.
It wasn't like

00:08:25.467 --> 00:08:27.434
singing in a sketch
or, you know...

00:08:27.434 --> 00:08:29.934
-Doing a bit.
-It was -- It was earnest,

00:08:29.934 --> 00:08:32.634
you know,
singing in a meaningful way.

00:08:32.634 --> 00:08:34.100
And so had to do
all this training

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:36.200
and seven weeks
of rehearsals, and...

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:39.300
But you -- I mean, Jimmy,
you obviously sing a lot...

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:40.367
-Yeah.
-...in your stuff.

00:08:40.367 --> 00:08:42.167
Do you do vocal training at all?

00:08:42.167 --> 00:08:44.467
That's what I found fascinating,
some of the...

00:08:44.467 --> 00:08:46.200
-Oh.
-Did you ever -- did you ever --

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:48.801
Did you --
Do you do warm-up stuff at all?

00:08:48.801 --> 00:08:51.567
-No.
-Did you ever do lion's pose?

00:08:51.567 --> 00:08:53.200
-No. What's that?
-Lion's pose.

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:56.734
You start here.

00:08:56.734 --> 00:08:59.801
[ Laughter ]

00:08:59.801 --> 00:09:01.033
[ Applause ]

00:09:01.033 --> 00:09:03.434
-Uh-huh.
-And then bring it back.

00:09:03.434 --> 00:09:05.400
-Mm-hmm.
-And then again.

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:07.100
[ Laughter ]

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:08.334
And then bring it back.

00:09:08.334 --> 00:09:10.434
Mm-hmm.
Then another lion's pose.

00:09:10.434 --> 00:09:11.834
[ Laughter ]

00:09:11.834 --> 00:09:14.901
-I'm sorry, the Bengal tiger's
